Issue #12, item X1 -- mutation evidence
crates/rtsp-restream/src/session.rs, requests_tcp_interleaved_transport

Mutation: removed the TCP-only transport gate. The real implementation
parses the request's `Transport` header and returns true only when it names
`RTP/AVP` over TCP; the mutated version ignored the request entirely and
unconditionally returned `true`, so a `SETUP` with a UDP `Transport:` header
would be wrongly accepted instead of rejected with `461 Unsupported
Transport`.

Real code (restored after this evidence was captured):

    fn requests_tcp_interleaved_transport(request: &Request<Vec<u8>>) -> bool {
        let Ok(Some(transports)) = request.typed_header::<headers::Transports>() else {
            return false;
        };
        transports.iter().any(|transport| {
            matches!(
                transport,
                Transport::Rtp(rtp)
                    if rtp.profile == RtpProfile::Avp
                        && rtp.lower_transport == Some(RtpLowerTransport::Tcp)
            )
        })
    }

Mutated code (transient, in place only for the FAIL run below):

    fn requests_tcp_interleaved_transport(_request: &Request<Vec<u8>>) -> bool {
        true
    }

